# VS Code Commands & Shortcuts

## Comment Shortcuts
| Action | Windows/Linux | macOS |
|--------|--------------|-------|
| Toggle single-line comment | `Ctrl + /` | `Cmd + /` |
| Toggle block comment | `Shift + Alt + A` | `Shift + Option + A` |
| Add JSDoc comment (above a function) | Type `/**` and press `Enter` | Type `/**` and press `Enter` |

## Common Editing Shortcuts
| Action | Shortcut |
|--------|----------|
| Copy line up/down | `Shift + Alt + ↑/↓` |
| Move line up/down | `Alt + ↑/↓` |
| Duplicate selection | `Ctrl + D` |
| Find & Replace | `Ctrl + H` |
| Format document | `Shift + Alt + F` |
| Indent / Outdent line | `Ctrl + ]` / `Ctrl + [` |
| Toggle word wrap | `Alt + Z` |
| Multi-cursor | `Ctrl + Alt + ↑/↓` |
| Select all occurrences | `Ctrl + Shift + L` |
| Go to line | `Ctrl + G` |
| Open command palette | `Ctrl + Shift + P` |
| Open file | `Ctrl + P` |
| Toggle sidebar | `Ctrl + B` |
| Split editor | `Ctrl + \` |
| Close editor tab | `Ctrl + W` |

## Comment Types in JavaScript (from Comments.js)
```js
// Single-line comment — used for short explanations

/*
   Multi-line comment — used for longer explanations
   spanning multiple lines
*/

/**
 * JSDoc comment — used to document functions,
 * parameters, and return values
 */
```
